{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q15405285","formula":"C₁₂H₁₅NO","hill":"C12H15NO","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":12.0,"H":15.0,"N":1.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"6-MAPB"},"descriptions":{"en":"6-MAPB (1-(benzofuran-6-yl)-N-methylpropan-2-amine) is an entactogen of the benzofuran family which is structurally related to 6-APB and MDMA. It is known to be a serotonin releasing agent and, unlike MDMA, a potent serotonin 5-HT1B receptor agonist. The drug is not known to have been widely sold as a \"designer drug\" but has been detected in analytical samples taken from individuals hospitalised after using drug combinations that included other benzofuran derivatives. 6-MAPB was first encountered as a novel designer drug in 2013 and described in the scientific literature in 2014."},"fame":6,"pubchemCid":122202866,"mass":189.25,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(CC1=CC2=C(C=C1)C=CO2)NC","inchikey":"QLAAURQYEAEHBO-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-(1-benzofuran-6-yl)-N-methylpropan-2-amine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"122202866","atoms":29,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.627,"y":1.748,"z":-0.155,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.98,"y":0.285,"z":-0.45,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.135,"y":-0.704,"z":0.389,"el":"C"},{"x":0.337,"y":-0.704,"z":0.035,"el":"C"},{"x":1.264,"y":-0.089,"z":0.894,"el":"C"},{"x":2.601,"y":-0.118,"z":0.506,"el":"C"},{"x":3.063,"y":-0.711,"z":-0.663,"el":"C"},{"x":2.131,"y":-1.324,"z":-1.516,"el":"C"},{"x":0.775,"y":-1.312,"z":-1.154,"el":"C"},{"x":4.469,"y":-0.512,"z":-0.667,"el":"C"},{"x":4.767,"y":0.18,"z":0.485,"el":"C"},{"x":3.639,"y":0.423,"z":1.203,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.432,"y":0.044,"z":-0.33,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.986,"y":0.249,"z":1.001,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.605,"y":1.975,"z":-0.477,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.698,"y":1.979,"z":0.913,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.292,"y